PRETABLE -- #529 kill table 5 (TARGETED), written BEFORE the table (mtime is the order proof)
Instrument: regress/crime_width_probe.py after the SECOND closing pass's repair (repair 6), frozen by the driver as
crime_width_probe.table5.py -- 121 rows emitted (87 row() call sites by the ast deriver; table 4: 77 sites / 111 rows).
First measurements (L1): ../probe_first7_fix.out 120/121 on the FIXED build -- `top rd2 v0' read 0x11112222, a
construction bug of mine: its lh loaded into t0, the register st() uses for every store VALUE, so the session's later
`sw 0x11112222' overwrote it before the print.  Moved to s3 (free in that session); re-measured in
../probe_first8_fix.out before this table (the driver's BASE run is the second measurement).

WHAT CHANGED SINCE TABLE 4, and the finding that bought each (panel_20260913_164716 + the Opus second-closing seat)
  BIT = 0x10000001 (was 0x10000000)   a decline answering THE REGISTER at INTSTAT/INTMASK passed: their low bytes were 0
                                      (kimi CLI)
  dog session: DOG seeded; + lh +0x30 (dog lh v0)   the same at DOG (kimi CLI); `odata = 0x100' at DOG passed the
                                      lb-only row (codex)
  imask: + ld +0x18 read-back (imask keeps)   a landing that ORs into INTMASK kept bit 28 (kimi CLI, glm)
  imask, istat, sh08b: + a follow-up refusal at +0x07   a latch keyed on ONE label (codex)
  latch x5 prologue: + lw +0x00   a pre-set in the REV arm -- the open member of glm's arm pre-set class (glm's own
                                      INTMASK-arm candidate is REFUTED on reading: the IRQ sessions' sd +0x18 precedes)
  rearm: CONTROL write 0x0201, REV read from the PROM window, + sw +0x04   re-arm in CONTROL's DOG branch (codex), and the
                                      same class's other branches
  top: + lh +0x27a (top rd2 v0)       a 2-byte refused read >= 0x200 answering the register (Opus, measured 111/111)
  mid session (new, +0x1f8..0x1ff)    no refused access set address bits 7 or 8 (kimi-k3:cloud): answer, landing,
                                      notice, fall-through, re-arm, latch keyed on those bits
  header: CONTRACT 3/4/6/7/8/9 + DISCLOSED rewritten; TIME assumption wording (deepseek, codex); gate comment (grok)

WARRANT FOR TARGETING, by table 4's rule (re-run an earlier kill iff EVERY row it reddened sits in a changed session).
